# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env.open — the OPEN-WEIGHTS configuration
#
# The same system, pointed at open models served by Hugging Face Inference Providers.
# Nothing else changes: no code, no image, no compose file, no migration. Diff this against
# `.env.openai` — the diff IS the answer to DPG indicator 4.
#
# ⚠ SECRETS ARE EMPTY HERE ON PURPOSE. This file is tracked. `LLM_API_KEY` is a Hugging Face
#    token (`hf_…`); it belongs in `env.local`, which is gitignored.
#
# ⚠ STATUS — read this before quoting the file as evidence (updated 2026-08-27):
#    The model ids below are still PLACEHOLDERS: DPG-23 has NOT chosen a model, which was its
#    whole point. What HAS been measured since this block first said "unmeasured as of
#    2026-08-18" — do not repeat that line, it is out of date:
#      ✅ CAPABILITY (DPG-21, 2026-08-20). `openai/gpt-oss-20b` passes all six probes and
#         HONOURS `json_schema` — proved, not assumed — at 0.73 s on the probe. Its licence is
#         verified apache-2.0 from the model card. The full matrix is in
#         docs/dpg/open-model-configuration.md, and the profiles it produced are in _PROFILES.
#      ✅ THE SUITE RUNS. 4 passed, 1 xfailed, exit 0 against this configuration, both LLM
#         surfaces, real calls (DPG-24). The xfail is the ASR endpoint below.
#      ❌ NEPALI QUALITY. The open column of the benchmark is 2 of 105 classification items —
#         the ~20,700-char prompt tripped the provider's token limit, then the account hit a
#         rate limit (D-50). Detection completed with a 0.000 false-alarm rate, which must NOT
#         be read as a win: the committed set has no SEAH positives, so a detector that flags
#         nothing scores perfectly.
#      ❌ ASR. Word error rate is unmeasured and blocked twice — the benchmark set has no
#         audio, AND the ASR endpoint below does not exist (D-53). See the ASR_BASE_URL note.
#      ⚠  LICENCE CORRECTION: whisper-large-v3-turbo is MIT, not apache-2.0, as several
#         documents claimed until 2026-08-27. Both pass the filter; the claim was still wrong.
#    ✅ Q-19 is ANSWERED (2026-08-20): the work is funded to a few hundred USD, owner-paid, an
#       envelope SHARED with the pilot's own inference. It no longer gates anything; the open
#       column is blocked on D-50, not on money.
#    **Do not present this file as "the configuration Nepal runs" until DPG-23 reports.**
#
# ⚠ `model:provider` — the router picks a partner PER REQUEST unless the id names one
#    (e.g. `openai/gpt-oss-120b:groq`). Production must pin a provider, because otherwise the
#    company processing a given grievance is not knowable in advance. CI may route freely: it
#    sends synthetic data only. Same variable, two environments, one line each.
#    See docs/dpg/privacy-assessment.md F-17 and 00_compliance_status.md §4.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

LLM_BASE_URL=https://router.huggingface.co/v1
LLM_API_KEY=
LLM_TIMEOUT=600.0
LLM_MAX_RETRIES=2
# Guided decoding is available from most router partners; clamp this down if yours lacks it.
LLM_STRUCTURED_OUTPUT=json_schema

# Whisper-class ASR is served by the same router; give it its own, longer deadline.
#
# 🔴 **D-53 — THIS ENDPOINT DOES NOT EXIST, and the value below is kept deliberately.**
#    Verified 2026-08-20: `https://router.huggingface.co/v1` serves NO `/v1/audio/*` route.
#    `POST /v1/audio/transcriptions` returns 404 for every ASR model id tried, including a
#    provider-pinned form. So the committed open configuration **cannot transcribe** — this is
#    the one line of `.env.open` that is not merely unmeasured but wrong.
#    It is left in place rather than blanked because blanking it would make the failure silent;
#    a live test xfails on it with `strict=True`, so the day someone fixes the route the suite
#    goes red and this comment gets deleted with it.
#    ⚠ Nothing in production breaks: voice transcription is parked (PARKED_TASKS, DPG-19b).
#    Followup: docs/sprints/2026-08-llm/followups/the-open-config-has-no-working-asr-endpoint.md
ASR_BASE_URL=https://router.huggingface.co/v1
ASR_API_KEY=
ASR_TIMEOUT=900

# ⚠ PLACEHOLDERS — DPG-23 replaces these with measured choices.
# ⭐ TWO MODELS — decided by the owner 2026-08-20, mirroring the closed configuration.
# One text model for every text task, one for transcription. Benchmark many candidates
# (DPG-23); ship two. Every MODEL_* below except MODEL_ASR must therefore carry the SAME
# value — a per-task split is a decision to re-open with a measurement, not a default.
#
# ⚠ The selection criterion that follows from this: with one model doing everything, you
# select on the HARDEST task, not the average. That is SEAH recall (a miss is a
# safeguarding failure) and the complainant-facing resolved summary (that text reaches the
# public). A model that classifies dust complaints beautifully and reads harassment poorly
# is disqualified, however good its headline accuracy.
#
# ⚠ These names are UNMEASURED placeholders. DPG-23 confirms or replaces them and records
# the date and the evidence. Do not cite them as a choice until it has.
MODEL_CLASSIFY=openai/gpt-oss-20b
MODEL_EXTRACT=openai/gpt-oss-20b
MODEL_TRANSLATE=openai/gpt-oss-20b
MODEL_DETECT=openai/gpt-oss-20b
MODEL_ASR=openai/whisper-large-v3
MODEL_TICKET_TRANSLATE=
MODEL_TICKET_FINDINGS=openai/gpt-oss-20b
MODEL_TICKET_FINDINGS_SEAH=openai/gpt-oss-20b

# The first attempt gets the short deadline because a person is waiting on it; retries get
# TIMEOUT_CLASSIFY, because nobody is (DPG-15b).
TIMEOUT_CLASSIFY_INTERACTIVE=30.0
TIMEOUT_CLASSIFY=120.0
# How long the conversation waits for the classification before carrying on without it.
# The grievance is already filed by then, and the result reaches the officer either way.
CLASSIFICATION_WAIT_SECONDS=30.0
TIMEOUT_TICKET=30.0

# Below this many characters (whitespace-stripped; internal spaces count), no model is called (DPG-19).
MIN_CLASSIFY_CHARS=25

# Leave empty: the model profile decides. ⚠ **"An unrecognised id gets the conservative default"
# no longer means "every open-weights model"** — DPG-21 measured four families into _PROFILES on
# 2026-08-20, so `gpt-oss`, `Qwen3.5` and `phi-4` now resolve to a MEASURED rung, not to
# DEFAULT_PROFILE. `openai/gpt-oss-20b` below therefore gets `json_schema`, which it was proved to
# HONOUR rather than merely accept. Anything not in _PROFILES still falls back conservatively.
# Set one of these only to lift a provider you have verified yourself.
#
# ⚠ Two traps the measurement found, both of which DEFAULT_PROFILE would have hidden:
#   * `Qwen3.5-9B` ACCEPTS `json_schema` and silently ignores it — 200, plausible JSON, schema not
#     applied. It carries a `json_object` row for that reason. Accepted is not honoured.
#   * `gpt-oss` and Qwen both REASON, and DEFAULT_PROFILE assumed a reasoning overhead of 0 — so a
#     model that budgets no reasoning tokens returns empty content. That trap was sitting under
#     this very file until _PROFILES gained the rows.
# Re-run scripts/ops/llm_smoke.py before trusting a model id that is not already in _PROFILES.
STRUCTURED_CLASSIFY=
STRUCTURED_EXTRACT=
STRUCTURED_TRANSLATE=
STRUCTURED_DETECT=
STRUCTURED_TICKET_FINDINGS=
